cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use oss-publish in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "oss-publish"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/oss-publish"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/oss-publish"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A publishing pipeline for opening internal work without leaking it. Personal data is
  replaced by plausible fakes of the same shape rather than blacked out, so the documents
  and code still work; substitution is sha256-deterministic, making re-publication a no-op
  instead of a diff full of churn. A fail-closed gate then re-scans the entire tree before
  the push, not only the changed files, on the measured grounds that already published is
  not a synonym for already checked. Files whose point is third-party personal data cannot
  be saved by substitution and are denied by name and by shape rule. Stdlib-only Python, no
  network, no telemetry.
keywords:
  - open-source
  - data-sanitization
  - privacy
  - anonymization
  - ci-gate
  - publishing
